      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:12 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jonathan S. Franklin (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FRANKLIN: Justice Stevens, and may it please the Court: The patent claim at issue in this case was held to be infringed whenever any doctor looks at a homocysteine test result and reflexively thinks about a basic natural correlation. The result has been multimillion dollar damages and an injunction prohibiting a testing company from conducting important homocysteine tests by any method and for any reason whatsoever."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The result has been multimillion dollar damages and an injunction prohibiting a testing company from conducting important homocysteine tests by any method and for any reason whatsoever."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is that second point -- is that second point definiteness?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Franklin",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It applies to any homocysteine test, no matter how it's done, no matter what reason it's done, no matter if it's in the prior art, no matter if I invent it tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Franklin",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I don't think the Court needs to get into the inquiry, and I don't think the Patent Office really wants to get into that inquiry either."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States Department of Justice",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Claim 13 satisfies the written description, enablement and definiteness requirements of section 112 of the patent act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you think about its validity under 101?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would you explain that in greater detail?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is LabCorp never asked the trial judge or the Federal Circuit to declare this patent invalid under section 101, which is an affirmative defense they had to plead in the answer and prove by clear and convincing evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Estrada",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Morse case, claim 8, it had been known for many years that it was possible to transmit using the electromagnetic current but nobody knew how. And in fact, this Court's ruling on page 107 says this was known by men of science everywhere."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The test for existing homocysteine was almost never used, as Dr. Allen testified to this. There is evidence in the record."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What has happened is commercial laboratory companies like LabCorp are selling the test to practice our invention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "in the prior art, whether you had an inherited enzyme condition, that would not be infringing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Number one, under the patent laws, everybody -- anybody who makes, uses or sells the invention is potentially liable as an infringer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What was made by man here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Would the case be different if they quoted section 101 in their appendix?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Unidentified Party Representative",
      "case_id": "2005-04-607",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8e14f67b26df95ffae023b1fecb05ab43b124081fa170eb8a04cde39c86811f2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8e14f67b26df-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "from their representative today is that they're not prepared to do anything about these kinds of patents unless this Court gives them further guidance. We are only asking that the Court give them further guidance on this patent and to say that a patent that claims nothing more than a natural correlation preceded by the inherent and generic step of measuring the input for that correlation is invalid and the judgment that is based upon it should also be reversed."
    }
